      "id": "emergent_federated_compute_pool",
      "description": "A coalition of mid-sized EU tech firms and national innovation agencies launches a distributed compute-sharing initiative, pooling underutilized government and academic GPU clusters into a federated network for public-sector AI development. Driven by sovereignty concerns and limited access to frontier models, it enables smaller actors to run high-capacity models independently. The network gains momentum as the US consolidation posture persists, offering a pragmatic workaround to dependency.",
